+    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\release\release-backend.ps1
+
+The script: checks `wrangler.toml` points at the real Worker `leestn-api`, database `leestn` and queue `leestn-transcribe`; runs the tests on your PC; **lists waiting migrations (read-only; expect `0004_transcript_timing.sql`)**; asks `YES`, then saves a full backup of the live database to `backups\` and notes the Time Travel restore point; asks `YES`, then applies the migration to the existing `leestn` database; does a dry run of the Worker; asks `YES`, then deploys the existing `leestn-api`; checks `/health` shows `1.5.5`.
